    {
      "bounds": "Selected private raw-trigger3/caller/threshold/callback source only; no accepted wire grammar, natural scene, physical semantics, crossing/dedup or whole lifetime claim.",
      "exact_excerpt": "The original scheduler has a concrete numeric trigger path for its own trigger-table row3, `BNLD`. Its compiled numeric handler receives a 32-bit supplied event integer and compares it with its own configured threshold. The selected actual local caller reaches that handler only after ID matching, a numeric-status selector, a record-value sentinel check and exact status `on`. On the handler's selected admission path, the original captured callback reaches the scene launch boundary. These are new selected source relations, not a schema-only name match or a counterpart inferred from BNLD conditions.",
